course: dictionary
lesson: 6326
title: Many meanings, one word
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and context tells you which one the writer means. The word motor can be a noun, an adjective or a verb. «A factory robot is controlled by a computer that drives motors in each joint» means a machine that turns energy into movement, like the motor in a fan or a toy car.
explain: «Toad's coach-house is piled up to the roof with fragments of motor-cars» uses motor in an older, informal way. Motor-cars means cars. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Car fits the sentence, so car is the meaning.
explain: Motor can also describe other words. In «motor racing» it tells you what kind of racing it is: racing with cars. In «motor skills» it is about the body. Fine motor skills are small movements, like writing. Gross motor skills are big movements, like running.
fact: A motor is a machine that turns energy, usually electricity or fuel, into movement.
fact: In the UK, motor can mean a car, especially in informal speech.
fact: Karl Benz built a motor car in 1886, so the word has been used for cars for a very long time.
fact: Motor skills are movements of the body, and they are split into fine motor skills and gross motor skills.
fact: A motor vehicle is a vehicle with an engine, such as a car, a lorry or a bus.
exercise: «A factory robot is controlled by a computer that drives motors in each joint.» In this sentence, what is a motor? | A type of car | *A machine that turns energy into movement | A loud noise | A small, slow animal
exercise: Toad's coach-house is «piled up to the roof with fragments of motor-cars». What does motor-cars mean? | *Cars | Motorboats | Bicycles | Aeroplanes
exercise: Writing with a pencil uses small, careful movements. Which phrase describes these skills? | Motorways | *Fine motor skills | Gross motor skills | Motor racing
test: In «motor racing», motor describes the racing. What kind of word is motor here? | A verb | An adverb | *An adjective | A noun
test: Which of these is an example of gross motor skills? | Drawing a tiny picture | *Running across the playground | Threading a needle | Writing a letter
exam: In «the Toad, the motor-car snatcher», what does motor-car mean? | Movement of the body | A road | A machine in a fan | *A car
